===Glyph origin===
First attested as the phonetic component of {{zh-l|*憐}} in stone carvings in a form ancestral to the small seal script. In the small seal script, {{zh-l|*舛}} is graphically detached from the {{zh-l|*大}} with the dots, which in turn is split vertically and interpreted as the unrelated {{zh-l|*炎}}; ''{{w|Shuowen}}'' erroneously interprets it as an {{Han compound|炎|舛|ls=ic|t1=fire; flame|t2=feet|nocap=1}}.<ref>陳斯鵬：《舊釋“粦”字及相關問題新解》，《文史》2019年第4輯，第5—18頁。</ref> In the regular script, the top further corrupts into the unrelated {{zh-l|*米}}.
